From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 21:05:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] soc: sunxi: sram: Add the A733 system control

The USB PHYs of the A733 share a 200 ohm reference resistor whose
calibration is controlled from the system control block: the resistor
calibration control register at 0x160 and the trim register at 0x168.
The user manual names the block but does not describe its registers;
the offsets are taken from the vendor USB PHY driver. Unlike that
driver, which maps the block in each PHY driver on its own, the
registers are handed out here through the regmap of the system control
device, so every user goes through one lock.

Add a variant that exposes only these two registers and raise the last
register of the regmap accordingly; the other variants are unaffected,
as their access table does not include it.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards; the USB2 PHY reads and
writes the two calibration registers through the regmap. On the board
with an NVMe drive, PCIe on the shared resistor kept working while the
USB3 controller was unbound.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/soc/sunxi/sunxi_sram.c | 19 +++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/sunxi/sunxi_sram.c b/drivers/soc/sunxi/sunxi_sram.c
index 2ccaeacf8c70..cec1d18961d8 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/sunxi/sunxi_sram.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/sunxi/sunxi_sram.c
@@ -329,6 +329,7 @@ struct sunxi_sramc_variant {
 	int num_emac_clocks;
 	bool has_ldo_ctrl;
 	bool has_ths_offset;
+	bool has_rescal;
 };
 
 static const struct sunxi_sramc_variant sun4i_a10_sramc_variant = {
@@ -357,9 +358,15 @@ static const struct sunxi_sramc_variant sun55i_a523_sramc_variant = {
 	.num_emac_clocks = 2,
 };
 
+static const struct sunxi_sramc_variant sun60i_a733_sramc_variant = {
+	.has_rescal = true,
+};
+
 #define SUNXI_SRAM_THS_OFFSET_REG	0x0
 #define SUNXI_SRAM_EMAC_CLOCK_REG	0x30
 #define SUNXI_SYS_LDO_CTRL_REG		0x150
+#define SUNXI_SYS_RESCAL_CTRL_REG	0x160
+#define SUNXI_SYS_RESCAL_RES1_REG	0x168
 
 static bool sunxi_sram_regmap_accessible_reg(struct device *dev,
 					     unsigned int reg)
@@ -373,6 +380,9 @@ static bool sunxi_sram_regmap_accessible_reg(struct device *dev,
 		return true;
 	if (reg == SUNXI_SYS_LDO_CTRL_REG && variant->has_ldo_ctrl)
 		return true;
+	if ((reg == SUNXI_SYS_RESCAL_CTRL_REG ||
+	     reg == SUNXI_SYS_RESCAL_RES1_REG) && variant->has_rescal)
+		return true;
 
 	return false;
 }
@@ -396,7 +406,7 @@ static const struct regmap_config sunxi_sram_regmap_config = {
 	.val_bits       = 32,
 	.reg_stride     = 4,
 	/* last defined register */
-	.max_register   = SUNXI_SYS_LDO_CTRL_REG,
+	.max_register   = SUNXI_SYS_RESCAL_RES1_REG,
 	/* other devices have no business accessing other registers */
 	.readable_reg	= sunxi_sram_regmap_accessible_reg,
 	.writeable_reg	= sunxi_sram_regmap_accessible_reg,
@@ -424,7 +434,8 @@ static int __init sunxi_sram_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (IS_ERR(base))
 		return PTR_ERR(base);
 
-	if (variant->num_emac_clocks || variant->has_ldo_ctrl) {
+	if (variant->num_emac_clocks || variant->has_ldo_ctrl ||
+	    variant->has_rescal) {
 		regmap = devm_regmap_init_mmio(dev, base, &sunxi_sram_regmap_config);
 		if (IS_ERR(regmap))
 			return PTR_ERR(regmap);
@@ -486,6 +497,10 @@ static const struct of_device_id sunxi_sram_dt_match[] = {
 		.compatible = "allwinner,sun55i-a523-system-control",
 		.data = &sun55i_a523_sramc_variant,
 	},
+	{
+		.compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-system-control",
+		.data = &sun60i_a733_sramc_variant,
+	},
 	{ },
 };
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, sunxi_sram_dt_match);
